      "FacilityID": 1000122408,
      "SummaryText": "The purpose of the Chemical Accident Prevention Provisions (CAPP) program is to prevent accidental releases of regulated substances and minimize the severity of those releases if they should occur. Under the CAPP program, a Risk Management Plan (RMP) is required for stationary sources that have regulated substances above the specified thresholds. These thresholds are provided in Section 68.130 of the Accidental Release Prevention (ARP) regulations (Title 40, Part 68 of the Code of Federal Regulations [40 CFR \u00a768] and South Carolina Regulation 61-62.68). Tables 1 through 4 of section 68.130 list regulated substances and their associated threshold quantities.\n\nOn behalf of ES Foundry Corp (ES Foundry), Haley & Aldrich, Inc. (Haley & Aldrich) developed this RMP to satisfy the requirements of the CAPP program."
    }
